nl80211_put_acl()'s "disabled" branch was fixed in 0007 (wrong attribute
type, a universal bug). This is the remaining half of the same underlying
problem: mac80211_hwsim advertises no MAC ACL capability at all -- no
NL80211_ATTR_MAC_ACL_MAX_MAC_ADDRS on the wiphy (confirmed: no "ACL" line at
all in `iw phy phy13 info`, unlike drivers that do support it) -- so even a
properly-nested, valid ACL_POLICY/MAC_ADDRS pair from the "enabled" branch
still gets the whole START_AP/NEW_BEACON request rejected with -EOPNOTSUPP.

Confirmed via a raw netlink capture (strace -x, decoded with pyroute2) on
the mesh_backhaul VAPs specifically: they're the only ones with
mac_filter_enable=true (see wifi_db.c's isVapMeshBackhaul() branch), i.e.
the only ones that reach nl80211_put_acl()'s "enabled" branch instead of the
"disabled" one 0007 already fixed. Both wifi0.1 (mesh_backhaul_2g) and
wifi1.1 (mesh_backhaul_5g) carry ACL_POLICY=DENY_UNLESS_LISTED with a
single placeholder null-MAC entry -- a well-formed, correctly-nested
attribute -- and both get -EOPNOTSUPP anyway, while their sibling VAPs on
the same radios (which 0007 already lets through, since they have
mac_filter_enable=false) succeed.

Skip the whole nl80211_put_acl() call under HWSIM_RADIO. Real BananaPi R4
hardware (which does support ACL, hence this code existing at all) is
unaffected -- the guard only adds !defined(HWSIM_RADIO), it doesn't change
real-hardware behavior.

---
 src/wifi_hal_nl80211.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
--- a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
@@ -17376,8 +17376,16 @@
         }
     }

-#if defined(NL80211_ACL) && !defined(PLATFORM_LINUX)
+#if defined(NL80211_ACL) && !defined(PLATFORM_LINUX) && !defined(HWSIM_RADIO)
     //Raspberry Pi kernel requires patching to support ACL functionality.
+    //mac80211_hwsim advertises no MAC ACL capability at all (no
+    //NL80211_ATTR_MAC_ACL_MAX_MAC_ADDRS on the wiphy): even a properly-nested,
+    //valid ACL_POLICY/MAC_ADDRS pair (not just the malformed disabled-case this
+    //file's other patch fixes) gets the whole START_AP/NEW_BEACON request
+    //rejected with -EOPNOTSUPP -- confirmed via a raw netlink capture on the
+    //mesh_backhaul VAPs specifically (the only ones with mac_filter_enable=true,
+    //i.e. the only ones that reach the "enabled" branch of nl80211_put_acl()).
+    //Skip the call entirely under hwsim; real BananaPi R4 hardware is unaffected.
     nl80211_put_acl(msg, interface);
 #endif
